# @NAME@

Scaffolded by [zide](https://zed.dev) - language: `@LANG@`, tests: `@TESTFW@`, strict warnings: `@STRICT_ONOFF@`.

## Quick start

```sh
cmake --preset dev
cmake --build --preset dev
ctest --preset dev
./build/dev/@IDENT@
```

Presets: `dev`, `release`, `asan`, `ubsan`, `tsan`. Helper scripts live in `scripts/`
(`build.sh`, `run.sh`, `format.sh [--check]`, `sanitize.sh [asan|ubsan|tsan|all]`).

## Layout

```
include/@IDENT@/   public headers
src/               implementation + main
tests/             ctest targets
benchmarks/        optional (enabled with zide --benchmarks)
cmake/             CMake modules
scripts/           build / run / format / sanitize
third_party/       dependency notes (FetchContent examples; nothing is fetched)
.zed/              Zed settings, tasks and debug profiles
```

## Zed

Open the folder in Zed. `clangd` reads `.clangd`, which points at `build/dev/compile_commands.json`
(run `cmake --preset dev` once). Use `task: spawn` for build/test/run/format and the debugger panel
for `CodeLLDB` or `GDB` profiles.

## Tests

`@TESTFW@` is used when the framework is installed system-wide and CMake can find it; otherwise the
same target falls back to a dependency-free smoke test, so `ctest` always works offline.
